Can you predict a feasible input without writing any code? Please reason and put your final answer in the form of a JSON object, even if the there is only one input variable, with keys strictly matching the input variables' names as specified.

Tip: Here is a reference code snippet for this question. You can refer to this code to guide your reasoning but not copy spans of code directly.

def main_solution(capacitors_parallel, capacitors_series):
    parallel_sum = 0.0
    for index, capacitor in enumerate(capacitors_parallel):
        if capacitor < 0:
            msg = f"Capacitor at index {index} has a negative value!"
            raise ValueError(msg)
        parallel_sum += capacitor

    series_sum = 0.0
    for index, capacitor in enumerate(capacitors_series):
        if capacitor <= 0:
            msg = f"Capacitor at index {index} has a negative or zero value!"
            raise ValueError(msg)
        series_sum += 1 / capacitor
    series_result = 1 / series_sum

    return {
        "equivalent_parallel": parallel_sum,
        "equivalent_series": series_result
    }
