You are given a string `s`. Your task is to compute the Burrows-Wheeler Transform (BWT) of the string. The BWT rearranges the characters of the string into runs of similar characters, which is useful for compression. The function should return a dictionary containing the transformed string (`bwt_string`), the index of the original string in the sorted list of rotations (`idx_original_string`), and the original string itself (`original_string`).

The input and output requirements are as follows:

