Given a rectangular area defined by its width and height, and a set of points within this area, how can we efficiently organize these points into a quadtree structure to optimize spatial queries? Specifically, what is the final state of the quadtree after inserting all the points, considering the maximum capacity of each node?

The input and output requirements are as follows:

